From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NomDeTom <nomdetom@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: clear scan_request when sending the scan fails

rwnx_cfg80211_scan() stores the request in rwnx_hw->scan_request before
sending SCANU_START_REQ. When the send fails, the error goes back to
cfg80211, which frees the request, but scan_request still points at it.
A late SCANU_START_CFM (or the next scan's completion) then calls
cfg80211_scan_done() on freed memory.

Seen on an AIC8800DC (Luckfox Lyra Zero W) with a command timeout
injected during a scan: the kernel panicked in cfg80211_scan_done(),
caught twice on the serial console.

The same change is merged in shenmintao/aic8800d80 as d910a71 (#116).
---
 src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -2930,8 +2930,10 @@
 	}
 
     rwnx_hw->scan_request = request;
-    if ((error = rwnx_send_scanu_req(rwnx_hw, rwnx_vif, request)))
+    if ((error = rwnx_send_scanu_req(rwnx_hw, rwnx_vif, request))) {
+        rwnx_hw->scan_request = NULL;
         return error;
+    }
 
     return 0;
 }
